<http://data.silknow.org/object/5810639a-36a6-3a66-b90c-2c0cd4ef7db3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin and cotton. Woven with a large scale floral meander in coloured cottons and silks on a white silk and cotton ground. In the meander are ears of corns, roses, berries and other fruit and flowers. The panel is half a loom width with a symmetrical design.\n\nBrocaded satin with the pattern bound in 4/1 twill by a binding warp taken from the ground warp threads (every 4th thread is used to bind the brocaded wefts). The warp is of paired threads S thrown silk. The weft ground of paired threads Z spun cotton. Brocaded wefts of floss silk. The width of the repeat is unknown."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/5810639a-36a6-3a66-b90c-2c0cd4ef7db3> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/5810639a-36a6-3a66-b90c-2c0cd4ef7db3/dimension/1>
