<http://data.silknow.org/object/5810639a-36a6-3a66-b90c-2c0cd4ef7db3>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin and cotton. Woven with a large scale floral meander in coloured cottons and silks on a white silk and cotton ground. In the meander are ears of corns, roses, berries and other fruit and flowers. The panel is half a loom width with a symmetrical design.\n\nBrocaded satin with the pattern bound in 4/1 twill by a binding warp taken from the ground warp threads (every 4th thread is used to bind the brocaded wefts). The warp is of paired threads S thrown silk. The weft ground of paired threads Z spun cotton. Brocaded wefts of floss silk. The width of the repeat is unknown."@en , "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin and cotton, France, ca. 1850-1880."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/f000e782-5b7d-3eb0-a588-9edb35057605> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin and cotton, France, ca. 1850-1880."@en , "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin and cotton. Woven with a large scale floral meander in coloured cottons and silks on a white silk and cotton ground. In the meander are ears of corns, roses, berries and other fruit and flowers. The panel is half a loom width with a symmetrical design.\n\nBrocaded satin with the pattern bound in 4/1 twill by a binding warp taken from the ground warp threads (every 4th thread is used to bind the brocaded wefts). The warp is of paired threads S thrown silk. The weft ground of paired threads Z spun cotton. Brocaded wefts of floss silk. The width of the repeat is unknown."@en ;
